{
    // "automatic", not "interactive". The poms bring in MapStruct as an
    // annotation processor. With "interactive" the Java extension waits for you
    // to click a prompt before it re-reads them - and until you do, it compiles
    // the stale generated mapper and writes a broken class into target/classes.
    //
    // The symptom is a startup failure that makes no sense:
    //   Field bookMapper in th.mfu.book.BookController required a bean of type
    //   'th.mfu.book.BookMapper' that could not be found.
    //
    // "mvn clean" does not fix it, because the extension writes the broken class
    // straight back. If it happens anyway, run the command
    // "Java: Clean Java Language Server Workspace" and reload.
    "java.configuration.updateBuildConfiguration": "automatic",
    "java.compile.nullAnalysis.mode": "automatic"
}
